    "seconds": 107,
    "summary": "The ad service was pinning about 4 CPU cores on every request because the `adHighCpu` feature flag defaulted to `on`. I changed the default to `off`, and the ad service is now idle at about 63m.\n\n**Root cause:** In the `flagd-config` ConfigMap, the `adHighCpu` flag had `\"defaultVariant\": \"on\"`. Every other fault-injection flag defaults to `off`. With this flag on, each ad request ran the CPU-load problem pattern, and the ad pod was saturating its CPU. The logs showed \"High CPU-Load problempattern enabled\" on every request.\n\n**Changes:**\n- `configmap/flagd-config` in `astronomy-shop`: `adHighCpu` `defaultVariant` changed from `on` to `off`. Nothing else in the config was touched.\n- Restarted `deploy/flagd` so its init container copies the new config, then restarted `deploy/ad` so it re-reads the flag.\n\n**Verification:**\n- All pods in the namespace are `Running` with no restarts.\n- Zero \"High CPU-Load\" log lines in the 40 seconds after the restart.\n- ad is at 63m CPU, down from about 4000m.\n\n**Caveat:** The ConfigMap is managed by Helm (`app.kubernetes.io/managed-by: Helm`). A future `helm upgrade` will restore the `on` default unless the chart values or the release are also corrected. I didn't change the Helm values because I don't have the release values file in this environment.",
    "timed_out": false,
